## RESOLVED 2026-08-24 - Whole-container ECC framing (format v3)
Implemented in Wave K: RS(255,191) coded control header carrying all
self-describing fields + RS-coded body covering metadata + payload + CRC.
v2 containers fail closed. See container-wire-format.md section 3.

## REJECTED 2026-08-24 - Signed manifest verification layer (Ed25519)
REJECTED on post-quantum grounds. Ed25519 relies on elliptic-curve discrete
logarithm, which Shor's algorithm breaks completely. The existing HMAC-SHA256
manifest authentication is already post-quantum resistant (symmetric primitive,
Grover's algorithm provides only quadratic speedup). Adding Ed25519 would have
introduced the sole quantum-vulnerable component into an otherwise PQ-safe
system. The design goal is purely symmetric cryptography throughout.

## 2026-08-23 - Full fuzzing + metamorphic testing coverage (all layers)

Goal: every module owned by seeded, structure-aware fuzzing plus explicit
metamorphic relations (MRs), not just example tests. Builds on the seeded
pbt.js harness and the Wave H fuzz/MR culture (npm run fuzz; CI smoke slice).
Track per-layer adoption; "done" = listed MRs/generators exist + long-run
fuzz script exercises them without finding open counterexamples.

Current: wire-format L0-L3 (conformance + 12 PBT), capacity scanner,
escapeHtml, vault structures, algebraic transforms, huffman encoder.

- [x] codec: encode/decode roundtrip fuzzing (random dimensions/quality/
      subsampling/restart intervals); MRs - decode-after-encode stability,
      quality-vs-size monotonicity, dimension preservation
- [x] automata parsers (marker-scanner, dht/dqt/sof/sos/spiff): mutated-JPEG
      generator (truncation, marker injection, lying length fields); MR -
      valid files unchanged, hostile input always fails closed
- [x] bit-streams: differential testing across BitReader variants on random
      streams (all three must agree bit-for-bit)
- [x] error-correction core: GF(256) field axioms as properties; RS
      roundtrip under random corruption distributions at tolerance edges;
      interleave permutation-invariance MRs
- [x] cryptography: AES-GCM/PBKDF2/HMAC roundtrip + AAD-binding properties
      (structural; CSPRNG prevents byte vectors)
- [x] vault layer: operation-sequence fuzzing against invariants (locked
      never decrypts, revision strictly increases, freeze holds); MR -
      clone chains equivalent to batch operations
- [x] batch embedder/extractor: carrier-subset selection MRs, allocation
      determinism, capacity-bound enforcement
- [x] scripts/cli.mjs: argument fuzzing, fail-closed exit codes
- [x] harness: npm run fuzz driver landed (CI smoke + scalable local runs); full corpus
Related: RESOLVED whole-container ECC framing entry (see top of file).


## 2026-08-24 - CSV import: Bitwarden card/identity item types
Bitwarden CSV exports carry non-login item types in the `type` column
(folder,favorite,type,...). Current importer scope:
- type=login -> full import
- type=note -> passwordless entry import
- type=card / type=identity -> skipped with reason todo(card-identity-import)

No meaningful field mapping exists yet (cardholder number, expiry, identity
fields have no SecureEntry equivalents). Options when picked up: map to
notes text dump, or extend customFields conventions. Track skipped counts
in import summary either way.

## RESOLVED 2026-08-24 - TOTP live codes never render in vault UI (broken)
populateTotpCodes (app/components/vault/vault-ui.js) runs but produces no
visible codes. Diagnosis:
1. SECRET ENCODING BUG: line ~595 uses
   `new TextEncoder().encode(params.secret)` on the Base32 secret STRING;
   TOTP needs decodeBase32(params.secret) raw bytes (see scripts/cli.mjs
   cliTotp for the correct pattern).
2. Bare `catch {}` swallows every per-entry failure (suspect additional
   algorithm-name mismatch between parseOtpauthUri output and totp()
   options) -> slots stay blank forever with zero console signal.
3. No lifecycle: no 30s refresh timer, no copy-code affordance, and
   .totp-slot/.totp-code have no styling contract in vault.css.
Fix = rewrite populateTotpCodes against src/utils/base32.js + totp.js,
fail-loud logging, interval refresh aligned to period, CSS + hidden-until-
present slot; pin with Node-runner DOM tests (revision-tracking pattern).
NOTE: scripts/cli.mjs cliTotp has the SAME TextEncoder-as-base32 bug
(line ~117) and must be fixed in the same pass.

RESOLUTION: codeFromOtpauthUri() added to totp.js (single Base32-correct
path; algorithm-name suspicion disproven - names already matched). UI and
cliTotp both delegate to it now, with logger.warn on every failure path.
Added TOTP field to Add/Edit forms with normalizeTotpInput() wrapping bare
Base32 secrets at the PasswordVault.addEntry/updateEntry boundary
(validateEntryInput rejects malformed values; lone-surrogate titles fall
back to a safe label instead of throwing). Display renders click-to-copy
code + countdown, single-interval refresh lifecycle stopped on re-render/
lock. CSS contract added. Pinned by exact RFC 6238 vectors routed through
URIs (UI + CLI), display/lifecycle DOM tests, and form-flow tests.

## 2026-08-24 - Camera capture (getUserMedia) + perspective-corrected QR decode
Current qr-decoder assumes axis-aligned, cleanly captured symbols
(screenshots). For phone-camera photos: (a) add getUserMedia-based live
capture into the card dropzone flow, (b) implement perspective correction -
locate the three finder centers, estimate the homography, warp to a flat
module grid before sampling. Both belong together; ship behind the same
feature. PWA target (Android + iOS).

## 2026-08-24 - iOS / PWA track: directory import fallback + app shell
iOS Safari lacks showDirectoryPicker and full File System Access. Needed:
1. <input type=file webkitdirectory multiple> fallback in the carrier
   import path (also benefits desktop Firefox), feeding the existing
   DropZone pipeline.
2. PWA app shell: manifest.json (icons, standalone display) + service
   worker for offline vault use on phones.

## 2026-08-24 - Master-password second factor roadmap
Tier B shipped this wave: optional TOTP gate enrolled during vault creation;
explicitly weak access control vs shoulder-surfing only (anyone with the
master password defeats it - disclaimer shown in UI).
NEXT (high security option, discouraged-by-default): WebAuthn PRF wrap
layer - session key additionally wrapped under a platform-authenticator
PRF-derived symmetric key. Real 2FA offline (secret never leaves enclave),
PQ-safe, ideal for the PWA target. UX MUST warn loudly: losing the
authenticator = permanent vault lockout. Requires metadata.kdf2 wire-doc
addition + golden vector regeneration.

## 2026-08-25 - QR decoder: real-world fixture robustness (open)
The decoder handles synthetic v1-v15 symbols correctly (roundtrip tests
pass) but fails on 3 of 4 real TOTP enrollment screenshots. Remaining
issues require production-grade CV preprocessing:
- dropbox/github: grid sampling misalignment from anti-aliased edges;
  needs adaptive/local binarization (Otsu) instead of global mean, or
  sub-pixel edge-aware module sampling.
- discord: anti-aliased edges break the run-length window matcher;
  needs a smoothing/median pass on the binarized bitmap before scanning.
- gitlab: RS block correction failure from accumulated sampling errors;
  likely resolved by fixing the above two.
Synthetic roundtrip tests (v1-v15, all scales, jitter tolerance, scattered
damage within EC-M) pass. Only real-world captures fail. The fixture
tests in test/security/qr-fixtures.test.js serve as acceptance criteria.


## 2026-08-25 - QR decoder rewrite C1-C5 (committed)
Shared ISO capacity tables v1-15 + encoder ISO conformance (C1/C2),
Hamming-tolerant format parsing with all-level RS (C3), adaptive
binarizer + cross-checked finders + basis-vector sampling (C4/C5).
Result: 853/859 suite, discord fixture passes end-to-end.
Remaining 6: dropbox/github/gitlab fixtures need adaptive block sizing
(BLOCK=8 too coarse for ~2.4px/module images); jitter x2 needs spatially-
correlated noise model; darkbg fixed by flat-block polarity comparison.

